HookExecutorAdminTest
├── given the constructor
│   ├── when the transmitter, the usdc or the vault is zero
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when a source has a zero messenger or burn token, or a domain is listed twice
│   │   └── it should revert
│   └── when the arguments are valid
│       └── it should store each source domain with its own messenger and burn token
├── given claim
│   ├── when the caller has no claim
│   │   └── it should revert
│   └── when the caller has a claim
│       └── it should pay it out once
├── given releaseQuarantined
│   ├── when the caller is not the owner
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when the destination is zero
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when nothing is quarantined under the nonce
│   │   └── it should revert
│   └── when USDC is quarantined
│       └── it should send it to the destination once
├── given setSourceConfig
│   ├── when the caller is not the owner
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when only one half of a source is set
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when the owner delists a domain
│   │   └── it should refuse that domain's messages
│   └── when the caller is the owner
│       └── it should store the new route for that domain
└── given setLocalTokenMessenger
    ├── when the caller is not the owner
    │   └── it should revert
    └── when the caller is the owner
        └── it should store the local messenger
